  "_comment": "Enum labels — the text that appears in a value cell. Highly concentrated: the fault-status set below ('présente', 'mémorisée', 'prés. et mémo.' and the 'spéci.' variants) plus oui/non accounts for a large share of every reading on screen, so these are the entries that make a fault screen legible in English. Renault's abbreviations are expanded to the same width class as the original, because the value box was sized for the French. Trailing spaces in some sources ('Pas de défaut  ', 'Court-circuit ') are part of the key and are reproduced exactly. Strings already in English (Reserved, Charging, Regeneration, Pressed, 1st..6th, Isofix, the Dfp_* fault tags, Lower/Upper transistor N) need no entry.",
